  "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{3}^{3}÷({2}^{3}+1)\\times 27} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{3}^{3}÷(8+1)\\times 27} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{3}^{3}÷9\\times 27} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{27÷9\\times 27} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{3\\times 27} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{81} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{9\\cdot 9} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{9}^{2}} & = \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
